"fc606030-824f-518c-b2c2-61a2081b0469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074594 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074594 #edb/ref 1061 136317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074594 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52f13af0-120d-5b46-804e-4c4cf45042f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074594 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074595 #edb/ref 1061 136320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074595 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "09ba6c04-edf9-59b5-bc27-8b2e2f8cd62a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074595 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075045 #edb/ref 1064 "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by the whole number.\n\nFor example, to calculate\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2}\n$$\n\nwe multiply the fraction's denominator by ${\\color{blue}2}\\!$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = \\dfrac{1}{5 \\times {\\color{blue}2}} = \\dfrac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nNotice that we get the same answer using a fraction model, and the process is similar.\n\n![](images/3f/3f1f0dddd115c0d820de4d79624bd87492e215a6c2de43071fda73a4a0684d77.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075045 #edb/ref 1065 8562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075045 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "fcf4ea8b-7765-55e8-b5c1-a10899bee9f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075045 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
